Z||000000||Philphine||10-27-2000||12:41 PM||||<BR>looking at a gt instrument cluster. if i got one i would lose my oil pressure guage. not a real big deal, i would get an aftermrket one (already have a volt meter so i don't want the console pod). but that would give me quite a few guages around me. actually i kind of like it. i am an instrument mech. part time (air guard), so it just reminds me of a cockpit sort of. how many other guages and controls have you added? <P>i'll also end up with driving/fog light switches, extra horn/light flasher switch (in my shift knob), and i may rearange my stereo so that part of it is in the over head light console.<P>ricey maybe...but fun.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-27-2000||03:43 PM||||If the gauges are useful and actually doing something, it shouldn't be considered ricey.. but the 5" diameter tachs that people mount on top of their dashes.. I think those are a bit strange looking, especially in cars with a tach.. speaking of which, my friend Paul used to have a 1990 honda civic, 5spd, and it had no tach!!<BR>(no offense to anyone here who has an oversized tach.. hehehe)<P>As for the stereo in the overhead console, Loki and I have discussed that before and I think it'd be pretty cool! We were just talking about mounting the face plate of a head unit up there, and running wires from the switches etc to the rest of the unit, mounted elsewhere. obviously this wouldn't work well with a cd player. (or cassette)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
